 2. 💵 Exclusive: Bessent compares Trump Accounts to GI Bill 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: JaMar Jones for Axios Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent told Mike Allen on "The Axios Show" that Trump Accounts will be the "most important benefit for young people since the GI Bill," Axios' Courtenay Brown reports. 

 🧒 Treasury this week automatically created Trump Accounts for more than 60 million children.

 Bessent said in the interview at the Treasury Building that about 8 million people already created accounts before automatic enrollment. 💸 Bessent said the accounts could bring millions of new families into the financial markets.

 He compared the lack of access to a "food desert," saying that families struggling to cover an unexpected expense are unlikely to open a brokerage account and start investing. "By creating these accounts, we are opening this up." 🪖 Bessent's GI Bill comparison sets a high bar. 

 That program helped millions of World War II veterans pay for education and training and buy homes. Go deeper ... Subscribe on YouTube . 

 
 
