 Riot officers face protesting students yesterday in northern Paris. Photo: Lou Benoist/AFP via Getty Images 🇫🇷 Student protests in France over school resources and spending have led to thousands of arrests and hundreds of injuries amid violent clashes between teens and police. What to know . 🚔 New York Gov. Kathy Hochul (D) said that the woman who accused members of a Cornell University fraternity of gang rape was "failed" by people obligated to protect her, including police and the county prosecutor. Hochul has turned the case over to state Attorney General Letitia James. Get the latest . 🍿 The combined Paramount-Warner Bros. Discovery company will be named Skydance, paying tribute to CEO David Ellison's production company that merged with Paramount last year. More from Sara Fischer and Christine Wang . 🏈 Tony Romo is out as an NFL analyst for CBS Sports following his July DWI arrest. The network said in a statement: "We thank Tony for his contributions over the past nine years and wish him the best moving forward." Go deeper . 
 
