 4. 🥅 1 sports thing: Goalie goal! 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Igor Shesterkin attempts a shot against the Tampa Bay Lightning last night. Photo: Bruce Bennett/Getty Images New York Rangers goaltender Igor Shesterkin last night became just the 18th netminder in NHL history to score a goal.

 His third period volley into an open net put the Rangers up 5-1 against the Tampa Bay Lightning, sealing their home opener victory. 🏒 True "goalie goals" are so rare in hockey because they require a perfect setup — including an empty net after the opposing team pulls their goalie for an extra skater in a desperate bid for a late-game goal.

